{"id":"99753669379acbbef8e1e4fd92fe09d421cc5701f7c302643be7979e058032d5","lamport":1,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-11-08T20:21:42.835735458Z","format_version":1,"kind":"set-field","payload":{"fields":{"description":"## Parent\n\nSub-issue of 215ee3.\n\n## What to build\n\nA deleted ticket never shows up as live work anywhere. In `ti show`, a deleted child is filtered from its parent's sub-issue list and a deleted dependency is shown greyed as \"(deleted)\". Dependency logic treats an edge to a deleted ticket as absent, so a deleted blocker never stalls a live ticket. `ti next`, `ti stats`, search, saved views and the TUI exclude deleted tickets. Undeleting restores the ticket into all of these with no extra writes, because the links were never removed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] CLI: parent `ti show` omits deleted child from sub-issues; reappears after undelete\n- [ ] CLI: ticket depending on a deleted ticket is not treated as having an unfinished Dependency by `ti next` and `ti show`; edge rendered \"(deleted)\"\n- [ ] CLI: `ti next` never picks a deleted ticket, nor a deleted sub-issue of a container parent\n- [ ] CLI: `ti stats` open/closed counts exclude deleted\n- [ ] CLI: search and `ti list` filters exclude deleted; `--deleted` still works\n- [ ] TUI list excludes deleted tickets (unit test at the shared query layer, not a TUI reimplementation)"}}}